{"name":"Aroma Blue","hex":"#96d2d6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aroma","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A smell; especially a pleasant, spicy or fragrant one."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aroma"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Odor","blocks":[{"text":"An odor or odour is a smell or a scent caused by one or more volatilized chemical compounds generally found in low concentrations that humans and many animals can perceive via their olfactory system. While smell can refer to pleasant and unpleasant odors, the terms scent, aroma, and fragrance are usually reserved for pleasant-smelling odors and are frequently used in the food and cosmetic industry to describe floral scents or to refer to perfumes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Jan_Brueghel_d._O._-_Allegorie_van_de_geur.jpg/330px-Jan_Brueghel_d._O._-_Allegorie_van_de_geur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odor"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/ALCOSAN_Odor_Control_Covers_%286926400399%29.jpg/500px-ALCOSAN_Odor_Control_Covers_%286926400399%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/ALCOSAN_Odor_Control_Covers_%286926400399%29.jpg/500px-ALCOSAN_Odor_Control_Covers_%286926400399%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Odor control covers at a sewage treatment plant: Under these covers, grit and gravel are settled out of the wastewater.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AALCOSAN_Odor_Control_Covers_(6926400399).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Beagle_sniffing_another_dog.jpg/500px-Beagle_sniffing_another_dog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Beagle_sniffing_another_dog.jpg/1280px-Beagle_sniffing_another_dog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Beagle_sniffing_another_dog.jpg/500px-Beagle_sniffing_another_dog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two dogs sniffing each other","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeagle_sniffing_another_dog.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%